{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>עַל פִּי ה׳.</b> The mission itself was not עַל פִּי ה׳, for He said to him ״שְׁלַח לְךָ״ — according to your own judgment, etc. Rather, it means to say that the mission from the desert of Paran was עַל פִּי ה׳ — the first journey from חֲצֵרוֹת. For according to the word of HaShem, blessed be He, He would not have agreed to send them at all, but because of the abundance of their importunity He did not restrain them. Even so, He should have delayed the time of the mission, for from the desert of Paran there are many journeys until near the land, and He should have sent them from another encampment closer to the land of Israel than the desert of Paran. But because this encampment in the desert of Paran came immediately upon their arrival from חֲצֵרוֹת, where the incident of Miriam had occurred, HaShem reckoned that since that event was so recent, perhaps the wicked would take reproof from it. And perhaps with the passage of many days they would forget what happened to Miriam. And what is written ״עַל פִּי ה׳״ refers to מִמִּדְבַּר פָּארָן and not to the mission itself. And some say that it was specifically from the desert of Paran, for from this place His wisdom, blessed be He, calculated that they would go and return within forty days, so that all those who would die in the desert would be sixty years old, and would arrive in full vigor at the grave (Job 5:26) — every one who was twenty years old and upward, upon whom the decree had fallen."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:40:56.122437354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}